ves  turns out she's kind of a cop so far I  hope she's not at the end another new  character who I think has made a bigger  impact in the front end of the story is  talking to a marquis and he comes in  after the first palace when you boot  kimochi des at a shooting Academy from  being a piece of [ __ ] but he comes in as  a school counselor and he is a perfect  thumb addict fit for persona 5 because  he is a counselor he  talks a lot about mental health and he  walks the characters through kind of  coming to terms with their trauma and  trying to overcome that and it's a very  comforting thing to have a character who  represents that and I'm kind of  surprised that the original game didn't  have that now that I think about it he's  kind of a klutz himself he's kind of a  goofball but he has a heart of gold and  his confidant round is very valuable  because when each rank you get extra SP  for Joker another change of confidants  is Gaurav kechi he's a major character  in the original game but now you have to  go out of your way to hang out with him  and rank up that confidant route I think  he's still a cop but so far his  confidant route it's just hanging out  with him and kiichi Joji which is kind  of nice but I'm hoping that it evolves  later on and gives a little bit more  backstory as to who he is especially if  you've already played the original game  for covenants as a whole there's an  extra element where the person you just  hung out with might call you right after  hanging out it's a little weird but you  do have some dialogue options in which  you can get two extra confidant points  so you can level them up faster now I've  mentioned key to GOG a few times which  is a new area in Tokyo you can hang out  in and there's a place called penguin  sniper which is a place for you to hang  out with your confidants or your party  members and you want to go there because  there is darts darts is an actual mini  game Hyuk is a style where you actually  use the motion controls to throw your  darts and you can call people up to do  that with them and what you get out of  it is ranking up your baton pass because  they're extra perks this time around for  a baton pass and we'll get to the combat  mechanics in a minute but at penguin  sniper you can also play pool pool isn't  an active minigame but there is  conversations that happen around  scenarios in which you decide to play  pool there's also a jazz club which is a  nice lovely place to hang out and  there's some sweet tunes that play in  the background that is also sung by Lynn  the singer for persona 5 soundtrack  which is a nice touch now that's a lot  of the new stuff on the social sim side  of persona 5 royal when it comes to the  meta verse and the dungeon crawling and  the palaces there has been some remixes  a lot of the new stuff in the palace is  kind of revolve around Joker's new  grappling hook this gets you to  different places within the palace so  there are extra rooms or some rooms have  been rearranged to be designed with the  grapple  in mind now some palaces have changed  more than others namely the 4th Palace  has a new sequence where you string a  lot of the grappling hook points to get  to the different areas in that room and  in all of these palaces our three will  seeds you want to find these because  they give us P boosts and when you find  all three of them you can convert them  into an accessory outside of the palace  once you finish it that recovery in sp  also helps you keep going in palaces so  you can have an easier time to do one  day dungeon runs and be a little bit  more efficient as you explore them it's  not just the design of the palaces that  have changed bosses have new phases as  well  the most memorable change has been in  the second palace where the boss spawned  different versions of himself that are  tuned to different elemental affinities  and with the game's combat system being  all about exploiting elemental  weaknesses the boss 