 low on health and then you will see  this utterly ridiculous sequence of  events after the first time you see it  you can skip it though because they do  take a little bit a long time but I do  appreciate that they are there because  the combat revolves around exploiting  elements a weaknesses you can be casting  a lot of spells and p5 R gives you a lot  more opportunities to keep your SP  topped off as I had mentioned earlier  raising your confidant level with  marquise gives you extra SP for Joker  and finding real seeds and palaces will  give you a slight recovery boost and  also breaking up your baton pass so rank  3 means you get an SP boosts when you do  pass the baton to that character and  there's a meat shop and keeps you Joji  so get your meats that boy got some meat  on Sunday nights only get your meat get  your meat Sunday night Kichi GOG keep  your SP topped off you know I'm saying  another way to keep your SP replenished  is through a bunch of new items and you  can buy them from Joe say hey probably  wondering who he is he's a little boy  who roams around mementos when you visit  mementos you can now collect flowers and  you get stamps which you then cash into  him for different perks and items so if  you collect flowers it works as a  currency just for that day that you go  into mementos and he sells SP items very  useful ones too with the stamps that you  find in mementos you can actually change  the rate at which you either earn XP or  cash in mementos which is super helpful  and makes visiting mementos a little bit  more worth it  there's also a few new variables like I  remember going into the third level of  mementos and it was very dark and you  couldn't see anything so it's a little  bit of a new twist and also there's a  new memento song I'm not deep enough in  mementos quite yet to know if there's  any other songs but I'm excited to hear  something other than  [Music]  you know I'm saying mementos isn't the  only place that has new music new music  is littered throughout the game and I  don't have many hot takes but I'm gonna  say that the new ambush battle theme  takeover is better than last surprise  [Music]  sorry I will say that takeover is a lot  more in Phatak and it feels like there's  a little bit more momentum building up  going into battle when that theme plays  but also you know going into a battle  without ambushing the shadow isn't so  bad after all because you get to here  last surprise again so it's a knight's  touch so you don't have to ambush every  enemy we do get a little bit of a  consolation prize there so those are the  big changes that I've seen so far in my  50 hours of persona 5 royal there's a  lot more that I haven't covered a lot  more of my new details they kind of make  the overall experience a lot more  enjoyable and it makes the  moment-to-moment a little bit more  dynamic because of how many more systems  are layered on top of what was already  there with persona 5 of course there's a  lot more I haven't seen like the new  palace or what the new semester is gonna  add or how the end of the game may have  changed in p5 are those are the things  they're gonna determine whether or not I  feel persona 5 royal is the definitive  version of the game I have a lot more  work ahead of me and so much more of the  game to play but I am gonna take a page  out of persona 5s book and take my time  and when I do finish the game you can  expect my full final review here on  GameSpot  [Music]  you  [Music]

